Z||000002||Areakon||09-14-2001||01:13 AM||||I have a set of Pioneers in my car (TS-A4103)and they sound like crap. A friend of mine has a set of the kenwoods (KFC-415C) in his fiero and they sound way better, both in low range and in high range.<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||RossT||09-14-2001||02:52 AM||||I have the kenwoods and they sound good with the stock stereo.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.onlinecarstereo.com" TARGET=_blank>www.onlinecarstereo.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tonker||09-14-2001||03:29 PM||||I listened to the Kenwoods at Future Shop and the sounded like crap. They had adequate high range but the low range was awful!! I just installed a new CD player and my fronts are crackling. I'm not sure if it's even worth replacing them after hearing the Kenwoods though. I really need the bass since my sub stopped working after installing the CD player.<P>The 6x9 Polk Audio speakers I listed to were sooo much nicer! I think I remember someone saying you could get 6x9's in.. Is this true? If so how difficult and what needs to be done?||||reg||1
Z||000005||artherd||09-14-2001||09:36 PM||||Best? Focal TC90TDX inverted Ti tweter.  5V series polyglass or 5K polykevlar midbass.<P>Roughly (very) duplicating the TC120DTX and 7K011DBL based studio monitors I use, I hope  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Not installed yet, pics someday. Gosh, there's SO MUCH to do yet!~!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
